From: Thorch contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: match Thor haptics to original Android

AYN Thor Android uses 1300 mV and does not set qcom,use-erm. The Linux
driver reads use-erm as a boolean, so setting its value to zero would not
disable ERM mode. Remove the property entirely. Keep period and braking.
Override the shared haptics node only in the Thor DTS. Other AYN devices
retain their existing configuration.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
@@ -7,6 +7,11 @@
 
 #include "qcs8550-ayn-common.dtsi"
 
+&pm8550b_hv_haptics {
+	qcom,vmax-mv = <1300>;
+	/delete-property/ qcom,use-erm;
+};
+
 / {
 	model = "AYN Thor";
 	compatible = "ayn,thor", "qcom,qcs8550", "qcom,sm8550";
